<title>USA: Northwest Airlines sets two-part debt deal.</title>
<headline>Northwest Airlines sets two-part debt deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following $250 million two-part debt offering from Northwest Airlines Inc was priced on Thursday, according to lead manager Goldman Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>BORROWER NORTHWEST AIRLINES INC</p>
<p>AMT $150 MLN	 COUPON  08.375    MATURITY 03/15/04</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.790  FIRST PAY DATE</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BA2   YIELD   08.415    PAY FREQ</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BB-MINUS  SPREAD  175 BP    MAKE-WHOLE CALL AT</p>
<p>						 37.5 BP OVER UST</p>
<p>AMT $100 MLN	 COUPON  08.700    MATURITY 03/15/07</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.952  FIRST PAY DATE</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BA2   YIELD   08.707    PAY FREQ</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P  BB-MINUS SPREAD  200 BP    MAKE-WHOLE CALL AT</p>
<p>						 50 BP OVER UST</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1675))</p>
</text>
